      "rationale": "GridCell retains both Fin rows/Fin columns fields and deriving DecidableEq. Whole product equivalence retains both constructor/destructor inverse proofs; named Fintype instance remains exact. Zero row/column cases remain empty types and require no invented positivity premise. Qualified GridCell.rowMajorIndex remains an extension of the own newly copied GridCell type inside the same new variant namespace, using the exact original BitMatrix.ArrayBacked.flatIdx provider. That provider proves i*columns+j<rows*columns; no new unproved indexing rewrite. Original whole-file docs describe its historical Runtime.Semantics namespace and external correspondence clients. The new GRWTSK variant is not a replacement for that historical provider and is never imported into398. No foreign-language execution/validation, runtime integration or geometry/topology law is asserted.",
